irect response to foreign military/technological pressure. Choice B (adoption of Chinese customs) was also internal cultural policy. Choice C (annexation of Manchuria) happened much later in the 20th century. Choice D (Commodore Perry forcing Japan to open ports) directly matches Lord Ii's concerns: it involved steamships, naval power, and the demonstration of foreign military/technological superiority that forced Japan to confront its antiquated systems. This event directly validated Lord Ii's warnings from 1847."}], "error_count": 0}
