creases. Let me check if I misunderstood something.\n\nActually, I think the question is asking about the relationship between tension and wavelength, and the explanation part. The correct sequence is:\n1. Tension increases (given)\n2. Wave speed increases (v = √(T/μ))\n3. Frequency is constant (given)\n4. Therefore wavelength increases (v = fλ, so λ = v/f)\n\nThe explanation should be that tension varies directly with wave speed, and wave speed varies directly with wavelength (when f is constant).\n\nSo the correct answer should be C, which says wavelength is greater AND wave speed varies directly with wavelength. The wording in the explanation part is a bit awkward, but C captures the correct physics."}], "error_count": 0}
