sted in women's rights.' This is too broad a generalization. The passage speaks specifically about the French Revolution of 1791, not all revolutionary movements.\n\nBased on the specific evidence in the passage, Choice A best reflects the observation that the revolution, despite being progressive, did not concern itself with gender equality."}], "error_count": 0}
