sts a large apartment which is bigger than some house, which matches choice C."}, {"type": "generate-note", "prompt": "Explain in clear English the logical proposition (∃x)[(Ax • Lx) • (∃y)(Hy • Bxy)] using the translation key: Ax: x is an apartment, Hx: x is a house, Lx: x is large, Bxy: x is bigger than y. What does this proposition actually mean in terms of the relationship between apartments and houses?", "style": "text", "out": "$explanation"}], "error_count": 0}
