y mass-society theory.\nC: the media manipulate 'the masses' as vulnerable, passive consumers - This aligns with propositions 2 (powerless against media influence) and 1 (media as tool for social control). It emphasizes the passive nature of audiences.\nD: audiences make selective interpretations of media messages - This contradicts the theory which sees audiences as passive and easily manipulated, not as active interpreters.\n\nThe best match appears to be C, which captures the core idea of the theory that media manipulates vulnerable, passive audiences."}], "error_count": 0}
