lly had less clear legal framework.\n\nB: R2P requires a call for assistance by the State in distress - This is false. R2P is invoked when a state is unable or unwilling to protect its population, not necessarily when it asks for help.\n\nC: R2P is less arbitrary because it requires some UNSC input and its primary objective is to avert a humanitarian crisis - This aligns with the information. R2P requires UNSC authorization (less arbitrary) and its main goal is to protect populations from mass atrocities, which is a humanitarian crisis.\n\nD: R2P always involves armed force, whereas humanitarian intervention does not - This is false. R2P involves armed force only as a last resort, and humanitarian intervention can involve force. The key difference is the legal framework and authorization, not necessarily the use of force."}], "error_count": 0}
