{"outcome": false, "goal": "  subject: college_mathematics\n  question: Suppose P is the set of polynomials with coefficients in Z_5 and degree less than or equal to 7. If the operator D sends p(x) in P to its derivative p′(x), what are the dimensions of the null space n and range r of D?\n  do not use query-web or semantic-scholar in your reasoning. use generate or think to surface knowledge, or refine to extract information from text.\n  choices:\n    A: n = 1 and r = 6\n    B: n = 1 and r = 7\n    C: n = 2 and r = 5\n    D: n = 2 and r = 6\n\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\noutput your answer in this format:\nANSWER: X\nwhere X is A, B, C, or D.\nFinally, say the answer to User: ", "plan": [{"type": "generate-note", "prompt": "Determine the dimensions of the null space and range of the differentiation operator D on the vector space P of polynomials over Z_5 with degree at most 7. The space P has dimension 8, with basis {1, x, x^2, ..., x^7}. The derivative operator D maps p(x) to p'(x). In characteristic 5, the derivative of x^k is k * x^{k-1}. For k = 1 to 7, k mod 5 is never 0 (since 5 is prime and k < 10), so k ≠ 0 in Z_5. Therefore, the derivative of any non-constant monomial is non-zero. Only constant polynomials have derivative zero. Thus, the null space of D consists of all constant polynomials, which form a 1-dimensional subspace. By the rank-nullity theorem: dim(P) = dim(null space) + dim(range). So 8 = 1 + dim(range), hence dim(range) = 7. Therefore, the nullity n = 1 and the rank r = 7.", "out": "$reasoning_note"}], "error_count": 0}
{"outcome": true, "goal": "  subject: college_mathematics\n  question: The shortest distance from the curve xy = 8 to the origin is\n  do not use query-web or semantic-scholar in your reasoning. use generate or think to surface knowledge, or refine to extract information from text.\n  choices:\n    A: 4\n    B: 8\n    C: 16\n    D: 2sqrt(2)\n\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\noutput your answer in this format:\nANSWER: X\nwhere X is A, B, C, or D.\nFinally, say the answer to User: ", "plan": [{"type": "generate-note", "prompt": "Derive the shortest distance from the curve xy = 8 to the origin using calculus. Start by expressing the distance from a point (x, y) on the curve to the origin (0,0). Use the constraint xy = 8 to eliminate one variable. Minimize the square of the distance to avoid the square root. Take the derivative, find critical points, and compute the minimum distance. Show all steps clearly.", "style": "text", "out": "$derivation"}, {"type": "think", "value": "From the derivation, we have x² = 8. The minimum value of D² is x² + 64/x². Substituting x² = 8 gives D² = 8 + 64/8 = 8 + 8 = 16. Therefore, the minimum distance D is √16 = 4."}], "error_count": 0}
